      ],
      "images": [],
      "copy": {
        "brief": "A uni assignment for Typography in Context: a magazine for visual communication designers, with masthead, covers and a style guide.",
        "insight": "While organising my photographs into sections, I realised there was a cohesive colour scheme that heavily contrasted against the mundane urban landscape surrounding it.",
        "pull": "Tags are acts of resistance to the increasing standardisation of urban environments.",
        "response": "I colour-graded my photos and masked the backgrounds to enhance this contrast. One spot colour per spread gives the range of street art without clashing, on a grid deliberately broken in key moments, where imposed order coexists with graffiti.",
        "role": "",
        "credit": "Issue 5 cover artwork, which flows across the front and back cover. Made from my photographs and extended with Photoshop Generative Fill (Adobe Firefly). Graffiti belongs to its writers.",
        "oneLine": ""
      },
      "steps": [
        [
          "ISSUE 5 · BACK COVER",
          "The back cover continues the street scene from the front, with the masthead tag repeated in the orange spot colour above the issue blurb. The masthead is a chisel‑marker tag that changes every issue. For Issue 5 the E becomes an epsilon, the Greek numeral five."
        ],
        [
          "STYLE GUIDE · 1.1 MASTHEAD · 3.2 LAYOUT · 4.1 BODY TEXT",
          "I wrote a style guide that sets the rules for the masthead, type, grid and body text, so each issue can change its masthead and still read as CYPHER. Issue 5 is the reference for every rule."
        ]
      ],
      "pos": {
        "edge": [240, -20]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "16-days-of-real-talk",
      "slug": "16-days-of-real-talk",
      "n": "02",
      "title": "16 Days of Real Talk",
      "sub": "Conversation cards & a campus campaign",
      "year": 2025,
      "size": "L",
      "kind": "project",
      "context": "Socially Responsive Design, UTS · with WAGEC via UTS Shopfront",
      "team": "Asterisk Studios, team of 6",
      "partOf": null,
      "link": null,
      "keywords": [
        "design-research",
        "workshop-facilitation",
        "editorial-design",
        "web-design-build",
        "design-strategy",
        "conversation-cards",
        "campus-campaign",
        "landing-page",
        "figma",
        "miro",
        "webflow",
        "gender-based-violence-prevention",
